From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:09:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] fast: on OpenGL ES draw into the game framebuffer; its
 depth rows

USE_OPENGLES (and the FAST_FORCE_FB test define) treat the view as never matching the render size, as __APPLE__
does: Fast3D always draws into its game framebuffer and the port presents it. ES reads depth by blitting it into
a depth texture, and drivers differ in whether the window surface's depth blits (Mesa's llvmpipe gives 0); a
DEPTH24_STENCIL8 renderbuffer's always does.

AdjustPixelDepthCoordinates in that mode: the game framebuffer's rows run top-down (drawn flipped) and
GetPixelDepth flips an invertY framebuffer's rows, so the depth read-back read the vertically mirrored pixel.
The y is pre-flipped (USE_OPENGLES / FAST_FORCE_FB only). Desktop builds that draw into the framebuffer
(an internal resolution other than the window's; macOS always) still read the mirrored row.
---
 src/fast/interpreter.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
index 1a90618..93f6faa 100644
--- a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -5537,6 +5537,11 @@ bool Interpreter::ViewportMatchesRendererResolution() {
     // Always treat the viewport as not matching the render resolution on mac
     // to avoid issues with retina scaling.
     return false;
+#elif defined(USE_OPENGLES) || defined(FAST_FORCE_FB)
+    // OpenGL ES: always draw into the game framebuffer (a DEPTH24_STENCIL8 renderbuffer), which the port presents. ES
+    // reads depth only by blitting it into a depth texture, and drivers differ in whether the window's depth blits
+    // (Mesa's llvmpipe gives 0); the framebuffer's always does. (FAST_FORCE_FB: the same on desktop GL, for tests.)
+    return false;
 #else
     if (mCurDimensions.width == mGameWindowViewport.width && mCurDimensions.height == mGameWindowViewport.height) {
         return true;
@@ -5813,6 +5818,13 @@ void Interpreter::AdjustPixelDepthCoordinates(float& x, float& y) {
         // the game drew straight into the window, whose rows run bottom-up (game framebuffers are drawn flipped)
         y = mGameWindowViewport.height - 1 - y;
     }
+#if defined(USE_OPENGLES) || defined(FAST_FORCE_FB)
+    else {
+        // the game framebuffer's rows run top-down (drawn flipped), and GetPixelDepth flips an invertY framebuffer's
+        // rows (height - y): cancel that, so the pixel read is the one the window path reads
+        y = mCurDimensions.height - y;
+    }
+#endif
     if (!mRendersToFb || (mMsaaLevel > 1 && mCurDimensions.width == mGameWindowViewport.width &&
                           mCurDimensions.height == mGameWindowViewport.height)) {
         x += mGameWindowViewport.x;
